                    {
                        "sense_id": "e90cc276-9dbe-39bb-9804-0553d16d386a",
                        "entry_id": "37f45c8f-7c72-35dd-bf7a-97d8bb89519c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Polyèdre ayant vingt faces triangulaires et douze faces pentagonales."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6fe860b-218e-4346-b3da-e858160de5a8",
                                "sense_id": "e90cc276-9dbe-39bb-9804-0553d16d386a",
                                "text": "Les trois polyèdres quasi-réguliers sont l’octaèdre , le cuboactèdre et l’icosidodécaèdre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1875465d-92a1-4098-875d-5b900e078064",
                        "source_entry_id": "37f45c8f-7c72-35dd-bf7a-97d8bb89519c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e90cc276-9dbe-39bb-9804-0553d16d386a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ikosidodekaeder",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60056b96-4c42-4f8c-8090-f5dbc967b007",
                        "source_entry_id": "37f45c8f-7c72-35dd-bf7a-97d8bb89519c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e90cc276-9dbe-39bb-9804-0553d16d386a",
                        "target_lang_word": "icosidodecahedron",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "icosidodecahedron",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95e96c7f-f0b2-3abb-9cfb-785a91fb765a",
                                        "entry_id": "9c4bd556-876c-3cac-85b9-5face7381632",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An Archimedean solid with thirty-two regular faces (twelve pentagons and twenty triangles)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b40822b7-a2f0-41fa-b88d-a6126c8e5c1a",
                                                "sense_id": "95e96c7f-f0b2-3abb-9cfb-785a91fb765a",
                                                "text": "[…]together to form not only regular polyhedrons but rhombicosidodecahedrons, truncated icosidodecahedrons, and such."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9e5b578-0bb6-4180-b7f7-13d1febe137b",
                                                "sense_id": "95e96c7f-f0b2-3abb-9cfb-785a91fb765a",
                                                "text": "1992, Jean-Louis Verger-Gaugry, Quasicrystals and the Concept of Interpenetration in m35-approximant Crystals with Long-range Icosahedral Atomic Clustering, A. R. Yavari, Ordering and Disordering in Alloys, Elsevier Applied Science, page 498,\nA succession of 10 concentric icosidodecahedra centered at (0, 0, 0), forming a geometric sequence (the nᵗʰ one is τⁿ larger than the first one), is also put into evidence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3ab8888-8316-472c-beb2-93f3dc2ca201",
                                                "sense_id": "95e96c7f-f0b2-3abb-9cfb-785a91fb765a",
                                                "text": "The edges of the octahedron form three squares; the edges of the cuboctahedron form four hexagons, and the edges of the icosidodecahedron form six decagons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e394260-ff47-438b-b45b-4afb91365fcb",
                                                "sense_id": "95e96c7f-f0b2-3abb-9cfb-785a91fb765a",
                                                "text": "Thus, there is a star octahedron, three star dodecahedrons, and fifty-nine star icosidodecahedrons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8491948b-7a5b-462b-a27f-8607a3458f64",
                                                "sense_id": "95e96c7f-f0b2-3abb-9cfb-785a91fb765a",
                                                "text": "The dark-gray (online: red) icosahedra are part of the B clusters, the light-gray dodecahedra of the B’ clusters, and the (online: blue) icosidodecahedra of the M clusters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51a53264-b2db-4cd9-8517-91e27205000c",
                                                "sense_id": "95e96c7f-f0b2-3abb-9cfb-785a91fb765a",
                                                "text": "Polyhedrons include prisms; pyramids; the Platonic solids, including tetrahedrons, cubes, octahedrons, dodecahedrons, and icosahedrons; the Archimedean solids, such as cuboctahedrons and icosidodecahedrons; and the Johnson solids, such as square pyramids and triangular cupolas (dome-shape)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5d7a8046-0ae9-4498-a551-3422ce3a23a2",
                        "source_entry_id": "37f45c8f-7c72-35dd-bf7a-97d8bb89519c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e90cc276-9dbe-39bb-9804-0553d16d386a",
